e":"Basic Land \u2014 Plains"},{"cmc":2.0,"color_identity":["B"],"colors":["B"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Flying"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{B}","name":"Swamp Mosquito","oracle_id":"4bb4844c-2678-45c7-8f5e-9cf185fd484b","oracle_text":"Flying\nWhenever this creature attacks and isn't blocked, defending player gets a poison counter. (A player with ten or more poison counters loses the game.)","power":"0","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2006-10-06","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Insect"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"The player gets a poison counter as a triggered ability on not blocking the Cobra. Killing the Cobra after declaring blockers or preventing its damage will not prevent the poison counter.","oracle_id":"456bbc0e-a648-481f-b37e-9996029556bd","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An ability that triggers when something \u201cattacks and isn\u2019t blocked\u201d triggers in the declare blockers step after blockers are declared if (1) that creature is attacking and (2) no creatures are declared to block it. It will trigger even if that creature was put onto the battlefield attacking rather than having been declared as an attacker in the declare attackers step.","oracle_id":"456bbc0e-a648-481f-b37e-9996029556bd","published_at":"2013-04-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Triggers immediately after blocking is declared if at that time no blockers are assigned to it.","oracle_id":"4bb4844c-2678-45c7-8f5e-9cf185fd484b","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An ability that triggers when something \u201cattacks and isn\u2019t blocked\u201d triggers in the declare blockers step after blockers are declared if (1) that creature is attacking and (2) no creatures are declared to block it. It will trigger even if that creature was put onto the battlefield attacking rather than having been declared as an attacker in the declare attackers step.","oracle_id":"4bb4844c-2678-45c7-8f5e-9cf185fd484b","published_at":"2013-04-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Afflict causes the defending player to lose life; it's not damage or combat damage.","oracle_id":"5c09d646-afea-4fd0-9752-04820b81cc5b","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Afflict resolves before combat damage is dealt. If this loss of life brings a player to 0 life or less, that player loses the game immediately. A blocking creature with lifelink won't deal combat damage in time to save that player.","oracle_id":"5c09d646-afea-4fd0-9752-04820b81cc5b","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An ability that triggers when something \"attacks and isn't blocked\" triggers in the declare blockers step after blockers are declared if (1) that creature is attacking and (2) no creatures are declared to block it. It will trigger even if that creature was put onto the battlefield attacking rather than having been declared as an attacker in the declare attackers step.","oracle_id":"5c09d646-afea-4fd0-9752-04820b81cc5b","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple creatures block a creature with afflict, afflict triggers only once.","oracle_id":"5c09d646-afea-4fd0-9752-04820b81cc5b","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature is attacking a planeswalker, that planeswalker's controller is the defending player. If a creature is attacking a battle, that battle's protector is the defending player.","oracle_id":"5c09d646-afea-4fd0-9752-04820b81cc5b","published_at":"2023-07-28","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An ability that triggers when something \u201cattacks and isn\u2019t blocked\u201d triggers in the declare blockers step after blockers are declared if (1) that creature is attacking and (2) no creatures are declared to block it. It will trigger even if that creature was put onto the battlefield attacking rather than having been declared as an attacker in the declare attackers step.","oracle_id":"69556f6c-c05b-4902-bac7-012f0ed81b75","published_at":"2013-04-15","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
